Description: PipeWire-native Roland REAC endpoint
 reac-pw puts Roland REAC stageboxes on your Linux audio graph. Plug a box into
 a network port and its inputs appear as PipeWire capture channels and its
 outputs as playback channels, sized and named from what the box itself says
 on the wire, with its firmware alongside. No configuration and no model list
 to keep up to date.
 .
 It can also be the master of a REAC segment, driving the clock so that a
 stagebox slaves to this machine, or a slave that locks to a desk's cadence
 and returns its inputs upstream.
 .
 The package runs reac-pw as a user service, without root: it gives the
 daemon the file capabilities it needs for raw network frames, VLAN
 sub-interfaces and real-time scheduling. A small system service keeps
 NetworkManager off the network interfaces reac-pw serves.

